1
00:00:00,050 --> 00:00:02,617
Ethers are remarkably unreactive.

2
00:00:02,617 --> 00:00:09,427
Sodium, alkalis, ordinary oxidising and reducing agents: nothing happens.

3
00:00:09,427 --> 00:00:11,809
That is why ether is such a good solvent.

4
00:00:11,809 --> 00:00:15,117
But the oxygen still has two lone pairs.

5
00:00:15,117 --> 00:00:22,812
That makes ether a weak Lewis base, and every reaction we study starts with the oxygen grabbing a proton.

